Hi Mike,

Thank you again for all of your help last week! I was able to successfully create the multivariate multiple PGLS models and compare them with model.comparison.

I would like a way to understand how phylogeny is influencing the results of each pgls regression, so I can discuss the relationship between my response variables, the predictor variables, and phylogeny.

Is there a way to get a lambda value for a PGLS conducted with lm.rrpp or procD.lm, similar to the value you get for the lambda transformation with a regular pgls?

If not possible with a lambda value, is this possible with a multivariate Blomberg's K statistic (which is what I think physignal() does in geomorph)?

Or when you calculate Blomberg's K or Kmult, do you only do so for traits specifically, and not an entire regression?

Thank you very much,
Eve

